WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:12.640
In many countries, people like Amina and
Brian help measure the quality of the
postal service.

2
00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:16.640
They are panelists: they send and receive
test parcels,

3
00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:21.640
and they report everything from their
mobile phone, using Telegram and the ONE
bot.

4
00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:27.830
This short guide shows you how.

5
00:00:27.830 --> 00:00:29.830
First, install Telegram.

6
00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:32.830
Open the Google Play Store, or the App
Store on an iPhone,

7
00:00:32.830 --> 00:00:35.830
search for Telegram and tap Install.

8
00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:37.830
Then open the app.

9
00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:41.830
How to set up your Telegram account is
explained in a separate video.

10
00:00:41.830 --> 00:00:46.830
Now open the ONE bot chat using the link
your manager shared with you.

11
00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:49.830
Tap Start or type /start.

12
00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:51.830
The menu appears.

13
00:00:51.830 --> 00:00:54.830
With the ONE bot, everything is done with
buttons.

14
00:00:54.830 --> 00:00:57.830
Tap the buttons. You don’t need to type
commands.

15
00:00:57.830 --> 00:01:00.830
If you have a problem, tap Report
incident,

16
00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:05.830
and type only when the bot asks you: for
example, a number or a code.

17
00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:10.830
If you are ever lost, type /start and you
are back at the menu.

18
00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:17.830
Before you confirm a shipment, prepare the
parcel.

19
00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:21.320
In the ONE bot, tap View pending
shipments.

20
00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:24.320
You will see the parcels you have to send
and where to send them.

21
00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:27.320
Write the destination address on the
parcel.

22
00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:31.320
Then take one of your labels and stick it
on top of the parcel.

23
00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:36.050
Now take a photo of the label.

24
00:01:36.050 --> 00:01:38.050
Hold your phone above it,

25
00:01:38.050 --> 00:01:42.050
in good light, up close and without glare.

26
00:01:42.050 --> 00:01:45.050
The whole barcode and the number must be
sharp.

27
00:01:45.050 --> 00:01:48.050
This is the photo you will send to the
bot.

28
00:01:48.050 --> 00:01:53.050
Every morning at 9, the bot sends you the
list of parcels you have to send that day.

29
00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:57.050
Parcels are sent Monday to Friday only.

30
00:01:57.050 --> 00:02:01.050
When you have sent a parcel, tap Confirm a
shipment.

31
00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:03.050
Type the number of the parcel in the list.

32
00:02:03.050 --> 00:02:07.050
Then take a photo of the barcode label and
send it,

33
00:02:07.050 --> 00:02:11.050
or type the label code. Your shipment is
registered.

34
00:02:11.050 --> 00:02:17.340
When a test parcel arrives at your home,

35
00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:21.340
take your phone and photograph the label
in the same way,

36
00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:24.340
in good light, up close and without glare.

37
00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:27.340
Then send the photo to the bot.

38
00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:31.340
When a parcel arrives, tap Confirm a
reception.

39
00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:36.340
Send a photo of the parcel’s label, or
type the alphanumeric code on the label.

40
00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:39.340
The bot replies: “Receipt registered.
Thank you.”

41
00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:46.340
If something goes wrong, tap Report
incident and pick what happened from the
list.

42
00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:51.860
For example: missing materials, a broken
parcel,

43
00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:54.860
a parcel returned to you, or a label you
can’t read.

44
00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:58.860
Let’s say a parcel arrives broken, wet or
open.

45
00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:01.860
Choose Broken or damaged parcel.

46
00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:04.860
It is recorded and you don’t have to do
anything else.

47
00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:07.860
If you can read the label, confirm the
reception as usual.

48
00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:10.860
Is the problem about a specific parcel?

49
00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:15.860
First open it in View pending shipments
and tap Report incident on that parcel.

50
00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:22.320
That way your manager knows which one you
mean.

51
00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:26.320
Holiday, illness or training? Tell the bot
in advance.

52
00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:31.320
Tap Unavailable days, then Declare
unavailable days.

53
00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:33.320
Tap Today or Tomorrow.

54
00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:38.320
For other days, tap From–to and type the
dates as shown on the screen.

55
00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:41.320
Check the dates and tap Confirm.

56
00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:46.320
Your parcels for those days move to
another date or to another panelist in
your city,

57
00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:49.320
and the bot won’t send you the morning
reminder.

58
00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:53.320
With View my unavailable days, you can see
or cancel them.

59
00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:58.320
Remember: future dates only, and at most
90 days in a row.

60
00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:04.320
So remember: tap the buttons, report
problems with Report incident,

61
00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:06.320
and type only when asked.

62
00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:12.320
Need more help? Tap Help or type /help to
open the full panelist guide.

63
00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:14.320
Thank you for being a panelist.
